// WebGLEngine/tools/ship/plainNetVariants-selfcheck.mjs -- UNNUMBERED (the version is chosen at ship time)
//
// Run: node tools/ship/plainNetVariants-selfcheck.mjs      (a few seconds: section 3 flies a tiny real training)
//
// THE GATE OF tools/ship/plainNetVariants.mjs: the plain-net control across architectures (brain/PLAIN_NET_VARIANTS_WIP.md, written before the library): MC (relu, the circuit's cell count as the width: 42 / 47 / 5 / 47) and MT (tanh, the weight-matched width), eight pilots a cell, read against the first round's kept REAL and MN scores.
// Built and gated BEFORE any pilot is trained on the rig; the rig run is a command (see the note), and nothing here trains more than a one-search, three-iteration smoke.
//   1 THE JOBS      64 pilots, names, ordinals 16 c + 8 f + k, search seeds 80000 + 10 x ordinal (highest 80630), init seeds 4811 + ordinal, none shared with the first round's seeds or the addenda's; the widths (MC 42 / 47 / 5 / 47, which are the circuit's own cell counts read from the extraction; MT 65 / 72 / 9 / 72); the spec parser and its refusals.
//   2 THE FIRST ROUND the real file brain/rig-results/plainNetStudy.jsonl: four REAL circuits, eight MN pilots and a references record in every cell, and its own checks pass.
//   3 A PILOT       runPilot on stub dives (the record, the seeds, the champion, eligibility, the audits read once) and on a real tiny smoke (one MC pilot on 4b-P, one MT pilot on 4b-E: the net, the activation, the weight count, the start check).
//   4 THE READINGS  familyCell on rank fixtures worked by hand (the first round's test unchanged on the 4 REAL against the 8 variants), the share kept, the variant against MN, an incomplete cell; the three verdicts (a), (b), (c) of the registration; the checks.
//   5 THE COMMAND   arguments, resume, a stale file refused, workers, the report and its refusals, --one.
//   6 THE SOURCE    pure but for the files it reads and the processes it starts; the imports.
// NOT CHECKED, said plainly: that any variant is good or bad (nothing is trained yet); the first round's own machinery (tools/ship/plainNetStudy-selfcheck.mjs holds it); the process spawn of the real command (the real child is exercised by the smoke command in the note, not here).
"use strict";
import fs from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";
